{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a Shopify Theme App Extension section that renders a SINGLE metaobject entry of type "bundle_template" as a product-like detail page.
    
    Requirements:
    
    1. Data Source:
    - Use Shopify metaobject: bundle_template
    - Render ONLY one entry based on:
      - URL handle (bundle.system.handle), OR
      - Passed ID (via query param)
    
    2. Treat Metaobject as Product:
    - Title → Acts as Product Title
    - Image → Acts as Product Featured Image
    - Description (rich text) → Full product description
    - Products (list of product references) → Bundle items
    
    3. UI Layout (Product Page Style):
    - Top Section:
      - Left: Image (large, responsive)
      - Right:
        - Title (large heading)
        - Description (rich text rendered properly)
    
    - Below Section:
      - "Included Products" section
      - Display all referenced products in a grid
    
    4. Products Listing:
    - Loop through bundle.products.value
    - For each product show:
      - Product image
      - Product title
      - Price
      - Link to product page
    
    5. Shopify Liquid Requirements:
    - Use:
      - bundle.system.handle for routing
      - bundle.description | metafield_tag for rich text
      - bundle.products.value for product references
    - Handle empty values safely
    
    6. Behavior:
    - Dynamically detect current bundle via URL
    - Example:
      /pages/bundle/<handle>
    
    7. Styling:
    - Clean Shopify product page layout
    - Responsive (mobile-first)
    - Grid layout for products (like collection)
    
    8. Performance:
    - Lazy load images
    - Avoid unnecessary loops
    
    9. Bonus (Optional):
    - Add "Add All to Cart" button (future-ready)
    - Show total product count
    
    Output:
    - Full Liquid section code
    - Include HTML, CSS, and minimal JS if needed
    - Ensure it's compatible with Online Store 2.0, are showing the total price as a this whole metaobjects price so remove individual price of the product sum of them and show as a price of whole mata objects, as we consider that all the product have the same type/name of variants so we need to show that variants on the above of the product list, can we show the first product all variant option below the total price of variants 
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase
  assign bundle_handle = request.path | split: '/' | last
  assign bundle = shop.metaobjects.bundle_template[bundle_handle]
  
  assign total_price = 0
  assign variant_options = ''
  
  if bundle and bundle.products.value.size > 0
    assign first_product = bundle.products.value.first
    
    for product in bundle.products.value
      assign total_price = total_price | plus: product.price
    endfor
    
    if first_product.has_only_default_variant == false
      assign variant_options = first_product.options_with_values
    endif
  endif
%}

{% style %}
  .ai-bundle-detail-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 20px;
    background-color: #fafaf9;
  }

